    "body": "### Problem\n\n`:edit` on an unloaded file opens with the `\"`  mark set to the correct value, but `:drop` resets it to its default value. This does not happen in Vim where `:edit` and `:drop` both behave correctly in this respect.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open a file and exit with the cursor on the second line\n   ```\n   nvim foo\n   o\n   :q\n   ```\n2. `:edit` the file and observe that the `\"` mark has the correct value.\n   ```\n   nvim\n   :e foo\n   :marks\n   :q\n   ```\n3. `:drop` the same file and observe that the `\"` mark has been reset to line 1, col 0.\n   ```\n   nvim\n   :dr foo\n   :marks\n   ```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe `\"` mark is not reset to its default value when a file is loaded with `:drop`.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.12.6\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo (9.2.1202)\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nFedora 44\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nPtyxis\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-16color\n\n### Installation\n\nSystem package manager",
